B.5 THE NECESSITY PREMISE — **FINDING G-1 (GAP)**.

Quoted (r6 rep1(a), master lines 2965):

> Only \(k=\lambda\) can raise it, and raising it on the class is what the
> recentering is for — it is what the next sentence's "new valid development"
> asserts, and it is what makes `(SEC-RANK)` strictly decrease at this
> transition. So \(k=\lambda\) is the only admissible height, and the index of
> \(L_k\) is hereby bound to the side datum. **This binds the height; it does
> not derive the rise.** That \(d(\Phi_{\mathrm{new}}(\rho))>\lambda\) actually
> holds at \(k=\lambda\) with the digit \(s\) of the repeated residual factor
> remains a root-preserving continuation assertion of the carrier, hypothesised
> by HE7.A and unchanged by this repair.

and (same repair, opening):

> `(REF-HT)` is forced, not chosen, and the forcing uses master data only.

The necessity for T < k ≠ λ rests entirely on "the recentering must raise the
value on the class". Three problems, all verified against the effective text:

 (i) The rise is NOT hypothesised by HE7.A. I searched the whole master for
     rise/raise language. The only assertion of a rise anywhere is S1.7 clause 2
     (line 526) — "for roots of \(F\), its generic evaluation value is attained
     away from that label class and rises strictly on that class" — which is
     about the TEST polynomial Ψ_{λ,r'}, an object the master never identifies
     with Φ_new at the product-1 branch. The hypothesis suite HE7.A actually
     names is "window, cap, frame, origin, residual-degree, accounting, and
     root-preserving continuation assertions" (line 657), and S1.8's
     root-preserving continuation paragraph (line 619) asserts root preservation,
     product transport and invariant composition — no rise. r2 rep5's S1.9 suite
     likewise. So the attribution "hypothesised by HE7.A" names no displayed
     assertion.

 (ii) The cited corroborating sentence does not say it. "the next sentence's
     'new valid development'" is S1.8 line 581: "The above-line perturbation,
     window, and cap calculations provide a new valid development." That asserts
     a development exists and is valid — which is true at any monic degree-D key
     — not that d(Φ(ρ)) rises on the class.

 (iii) (SEC-RANK) cannot supply it, and the appeal runs the wrong way.
     (SEC-RANK) is installed by r4 rep3 as a carrier HYPOTHESIS ("this master
     does not derive it"), asserted at EVERY product-1 recentering irrespective
     of k. It therefore neither entails the rise nor discriminates k = λ from
     k ≠ λ. At most, well-foundedness of W_C excludes an INFINITE chain of
     no-op recenterings; it excludes no single one.

Consequence, and why this is GAP and not CRITICAL. The BINDING survives as the
note's own stipulation — its own words are "the index of \(L_k\) is hereby bound
to the side datum" — and every downstream consumer needs only the binding, not
the necessity: S1.8B Step 1 as rebuilt needs h(w) = λ₂ (> T₂ by clause 1) to
meet LEMMA HE7-12's hypothesis, and r6 rep6's scope clause needs the same for
each increment before the HE7-12(d) fold. Assume k = λ and everything
downstream verifies. What does NOT survive is (α) "forced, not chosen" and "the
only admissible height", and (β) the r6 counter's claim that "No
theorem-statement change is made by this round … it adds no case and no
conclusion" — under the stipulation reading the master has narrowed clause 3's
product-1 transition and sharpened its (OCC) demand to λ ∈ H_lift(B) (which r6
does flag).

